*.md
# Documentation that stays versioned. NOTE: `*.md` above is a blanket ignore,
# so any NEW .md file is silently untracked unless un-ignored here. Paths below
# were updated 2026-07-21 when docs/ was reorganised into category subfolders.
!docs/README.md
!docs/operations/production-deployment.md
!docs/operations/postgresql-standby-handbook.md
!docs/architecture/workflow-change-log.md
# Operational runbooks, un-ignored 2026-08-14. These govern the build and the
# recovery of production, and handbook §2.8 pre-stages the spare VM with
# `git clone` — an untracked runbook never reaches the machine that needs it
# during a failover, and is in no backup either (New-SocConfigBundle.ps1
# captures .env, IIS and the service definition, not docs).
!docs/operations/production-deployment.windows.md
!docs/operations/deploy-and-release.windows.md
!docs/operations/backup-and-standby-handbook.windows.md
!docs/operations/backup-and-restore.md
!docs/operations/backup-vm-handbook.md
!docs/operations/backup-storage-decision-brief.md
!docs/operations/reporting-layer-operations.md
!docs/project-roadmap.md
# Deliberately NOT un-ignored: docs/uat/uat-*.md and
# docs/operations/grafana-wazuh-wall.md contain a shared UAT password and
# internal host details. docs/security/ (VA report, credential rotation) stays
# local because a findings report in a hosted repo is an attacker's checklist.
# Keep all of these local unless the contents are scrubbed first.
.claude/skills/03-exploit-development/scripts/payload_generator.py
.claude/skills/03-exploit-development/SKILL.md
